I don't think that polypiling should be restricted - but if you do, the
simple way of making it work is to make it affect each object in the pile
with only a 50% chance (50 is arbitrary here). In the case of monsters,
you could do the same, but have a message such as "the floating eye
resists", or some other message. If monsters become more intelligent, and
start zapping wands at you, then this could be applied to the player - 
"You feel momentarily different" (I forget where this is used).

Comments?

